=== Demand Simulation

On Thursday we will begin to introduce the supply and demand model of markets. There are many things that influence your purchasing choices. Economists break these things down into six categories: the price of the good, a person's income, prices of related goods, a person's tastes, population and demographics, and expected future prices. There are an equal number of things that might change the amount of a good supplied into the market: the price of the good, the price of inputs that go into making the good, the technology used to produce the good, the prices of other things that firms could make instead of the good, the number of firms in a market, and expectations about future prices.

We’ve avoided the question of how to choose where on the PPF to live. Prices can answer that question, giving us a device to coordinate choices across buyers and sellers (of carrots, spinach, etc.).

